---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SealDemo from '../components/SealDemo.astro';

const tiles = [
  { href: '#new-install', n: '01', name: 'New installation sealing', line: 'Protection from day one, before the first spill.' },
  { href: '#cleaning', n: '02', name: 'Cleaning', line: 'Grime, mould and residue, with cleaners matched to the stone.' },
  { href: '#sealing', n: '03', name: 'Sealing', line: 'Penetrating or topical, chosen for the stone and where it is.' },
  { href: '#stains', n: '04', name: 'Stain removal', line: 'Oil, rust, tannins and more, drawn out without damage.' },
  { href: '#stripping', n: '05', name: 'Sealer stripping', line: 'Failed, peeling or patchy sealer taken back and redone.' },
];
---
<Base
  title="Stone Cleaning, Sealing & Stain Removal | Spickle"
  description="Cleaning, sealing, stain removal and new installation sealing for natural stone and concrete across Melbourne and the Mornington Peninsula."
>
  <section class="band hairline-top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>What we do</h1>
      <p class="lede">Five services, one aim: stone that looks the way it did the day it was laid.</p>
      <ul class="tiles">
        {tiles.map((t, i) => (
          <li data-reveal style={`--delay:${i * 0.07}s`}>
            <a href={t.href}>
              <span class="t-n">{t.n}</span>
              <span class="t-name">{t.name}</span>
              <span class="t-line">{t.line}</span>
              <span class="t-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band panel" id="new-install">
    <div class="wrap svc">
      <div>
        <h2>New installation sealing</h2>
        <p>New stone has no protection the day it's laid, and the first barbecue is rarely far away. Once the stone and grout have cured, we clean off installation residue and efflorescence, then seal, so the surface starts life protected.</p>
        <p>For landscapers and builders we seal before handover: your client gets a finished result, and you don't get the call about the first stain.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="h-follow">When to book it</h2>
        <p>Soon after laying, once curing is done. Tell us when the job finished and we'll tell you the right window for your stone and sealer.</p>
        <ul class="covers">
          <li>Grout haze, installation residue and efflorescence cleaned off</li>
          <li>Sealed once stone and grout have cured</li>
          <li>Handover sealing for landscapers and builders</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="links"><a class="tlink" href="/new-installation-sealing">More on new installation sealing</a><a class="tlink" href="/guides/white-haze-on-new-paving">White haze on new paving</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="cleaning">
    <div class="wrap svc">
      <div>
        <h2>Cleaning</h2>
        <p>Dirt, mould, moss, efflorescence and general grime, lifted with cleaners matched to the surface: natural stone, concrete, marble, porcelain or terracotta. That matching matters: a cleaner that's routine on granite can permanently etch limestone or travertine.</p>
        <p>We use controlled pressure cleaning where the stone can take it and gentler methods where it can't, so soft stone like sandstone keeps its face.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="h-follow">On its own or before sealing</h2>
        <p>Cleaning stands alone if the stone is already sealed and just needs freshening. If it's unsealed, cleaning is the first half of a seal job.</p>
        <ul class="covers">
          <li>Dirt, grime, mould and moss</li>
          <li>Cleaners matched to the stone</li>
          <li>Pressure only where the stone can take it</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="links"><a class="tlink" href="/guides/mould-on-sandstone">Mould and algae on sandstone</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band dark" id="sealing">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Sealing</h2>
      <p class="section-lede">Two kinds of sealer, chosen for the stone and where it's laid. We test a patch first, so you see how your stone looks sealed before we do the whole area.</p>
      <div class="seal-grid">
        <SealDemo />
        <div class="seal-types">
          <div>
            <h3>Penetrating sealer</h3>
            <p>Soaks into the stone and protects it from within. The surface keeps its natural look and its slip resistance, so it's what we use on most outdoor areas. An enhancing version deepens the stone's colour towards its wet look.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Topical sealer</h3>
            <p>Sits on the surface as a thin film and gives the stone a matte, satin or gloss finish. We'll tell you where a topical finish suits and where it doesn't, before you choose.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="links"><a class="tlink" href="/guides/how-often-to-reseal">How often does stone need resealing?</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="stains">
    <div class="wrap svc">
      <div>
        <h2>Stain removal</h2>
        <p>Oil and grease, leaf tannins, timber stains from decks and furniture, rust, mould, efflorescence and grout haze. We identify the stain and the stone, then use the treatment that draws it out without damaging the surface.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="h-follow">An honest note</h2>
        <p>Most stains can be improved and many removed entirely, but a stain that has had months to set in porous stone doesn't always come out fully. We'll tell you what's realistic when we see the photos, not after the job.</p>
        <p class="links"><a class="tlink" href="/guides/oil-stains-on-bluestone">Oil on bluestone</a><a class="tlink" href="/guides/oil-stains-on-exposed-aggregate">Oil on aggregate driveways</a><a class="tlink" href="/guides/limestone-etching">Dull marks on limestone</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band panel" id="stripping">
    <div class="wrap svc">
      <div>
        <h2>Sealer stripping and resealing</h2>
        <p>Sealer that's peeling, patchy, yellowed, or wearing off unevenly, often from a cheap product or a rushed job. Putting a new coat over the top doesn't fix it: the new sealer only bonds as well as the failing one underneath.</p>
        <p>We strip the old sealer back to bare stone, clean it, test a patch, then reseal with a product that suits the stone and where it's laid. We fix other people's jobs as well as our own.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="h-follow">Signs it's failing</h2>
        <ul class="covers">
          <li>Flaking or peeling, especially where cars or feet go</li>
          <li>Cloudy, white or yellowed patches</li>
          <li>Water soaking in on some areas and beading on others</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="links"><a class="tlink" href="/driveways">Driveway sealing</a><a class="tlink" href="/guides/how-often-to-reseal">How often to reseal</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap book-row">
      <div>
        <h2>By area</h2>
        <p>Pool surrounds and driveways each bring their own problems, and moving out has its own deadline.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/pool-surrounds">Pool surrounds</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/driveways">Driveways</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/end-of-lease">End of lease</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band hairline-top">
    <div class="wrap book-row">
      <div>
        <h2>Book a quote</h2>
        <p>Photos and the rough size of the area are all we need to price it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/book-now">Book a quote</a>
        <a class="tlink" href="tel:1300220045">Call 1300 22 00 45</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--lede); }
  .tiles {
    list-style: none; margin: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) 0 0; padding: 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: clamp(0.75rem, 1.5vw, 1.1rem);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .tiles { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .tiles { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .tiles { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .tiles a {
    position: relative; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; height: 100%;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--strong); text-decoration: none;
    transition: background-color 0.25s, border-color 0.25s, transform 0.25s;
  }
  .tiles a:hover, .tiles a:focus-visible { background: rgba(33, 158, 188, 0.12); border-color: var(--teal); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .t-n { font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1; color: var(--accent); }
  .t-name { font-family: var(--display); font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.15; padding-right: 1.5rem; }
  .t-line { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.45; }
  .t-arrow { position: absolute; top: 1.15rem; right: 1.15rem; color: var(--accent); transition: transform 0.25s; }
  .tiles a:hover .t-arrow { transform: translateY(3px); }
  .covers { list-style: none; margin: 1.25rem 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.55rem; }
  .covers li { position: relative; padding-left: 1.6rem; color: var(--text); }
  .covers li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.55em; width: 0.8rem; height: 2px; background: var(--teal); }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0 1.5rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }
  section[id] { scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
  .svc { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem); align-items: start; }
  .h-follow { font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .section-lede { margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .seal-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(440px, 100%), 1fr)); gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem); align-items: center; }
  .seal-types { display: grid; gap: 2rem; max-width: 480px; }
  .book-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem 3rem; }
  .book-row h2 { margin-bottom: 0.3em; }
  .book-row p { margin: 0; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.9rem 1.6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .svc { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
